<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">2. Guidance that may be offered</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Depending on the written scope agreed for your request, Silicon Geek may help with:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:list {"className":"cs-checklist"} --><ul class="wp-block-list cs-checklist"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Understanding the problem statement and shortlisting a feasible project topic.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Breaking the idea into a block diagram, flow chart and staged build plan.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Sensor, controller, power-supply, driver and component selection with rating/budget reasoning.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circuit-reading support, pin mapping, interface logic and wiring review.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Code-flow explanation, pseudocode, sample snippets for learning, error interpretation and debugging direction.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Testing sequence, expected readings, multimeter/oscilloscope checks and troubleshooting checkpoints.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Report/PPT structure, headings, diagram planning, result-table organisation and references guidance.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Viva and demonstration preparation based on the student’s actual implementation.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Cost estimation, component sourcing guidance and safe build sequencing.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Availability depends on topic, current stage, deadline, required material and Silicon Geek’s capacity. A request does not become a booking until accepted in writing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">3. What is not offered</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:list --><ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Writing or ghost-building a complete graded project for the student to submit as entirely their own original work.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Preparing a copied report, fabricated results, fake readings, false screenshots or invented literature review.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Help during a live examination, online test, viva, lab assessment or any closed-book/unaided evaluation.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Logging into a student’s college or personal account, impersonation or communication with teachers under a false identity.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bypassing plagiarism, AI-detection, proctoring or other institutional integrity systems.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Unsafe mains/high-power instructions without qualified supervision, or designs intended to harm people, property, privacy or security.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Guaranteed topic approval, marks, project working, publication, competition result, internship or placement.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Where a request crosses these boundaries, we may refuse it and suggest a legitimate learning alternative. Read the <a href="/academic-integrity-policy/">Academic Integrity Policy</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">4. How Project Help works</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} --><ol class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Send the brief:</strong> topic (if selected), course/semester, guide instructions, deadline, current stage, available components/tools, budget range and exact problem.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Feasibility review:</strong> we assess whether the request is ethical, technically feasible and possible within the deadline.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Written scope:</strong> included guidance, session/delivery format, exclusions, timeline, student-supplied inputs and fee are recorded.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Guided work:</strong> the student builds/tests and shares clear photos, readings, errors or questions at the agreed checkpoints.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Review and explanation:</strong> we discuss what works, what failed, what changed and what the result actually proves.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Closure:</strong> final clarification within the agreed revision/clarification window and a student-ready understanding checklist where included.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">5. Information the student must provide</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>To avoid wasting time and money, the student must be honest about the project stage and constraints. Helpful inputs include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:list --><ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>College format, rubrics, page/format rules and guide instructions (with private information removed where not needed).</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Clear top-view photos of the board, wiring and power connections; wide and close-up images.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Code file or relevant snippet, compiler/IDE version, board/library versions and the exact error message.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Expected output vs. actual output, supply voltage, multimeter readings and tests already attempted.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Datasheets or purchase links for non-standard modules.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Any deadline, attendance/lab limitation or component shortage that affects the plan.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Never send passwords, OTPs, college portal credentials, payment credentials, private keys or another student’s work without permission.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">6. Student responsibilities</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:list --><ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Perform the learning, wiring, coding, testing, measurements and drafting assigned as the student’s work.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Purchase/arrange components, tools, batteries, PC, software, printing and lab access unless a future kit/service expressly includes them.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Verify every connection and rating before power is applied; stop immediately on smoke, heating, smell or abnormal behaviour.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Take dated photos, preserve test readings and maintain backups of code/report drafts.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Inform Silicon Geek promptly if the guide changes scope, the deadline moves or a component is substituted.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Prepare the final report/demonstration in your own understanding and cite all references, libraries, datasets and reused resources.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Follow institution policies and disclose permitted assistance where your institution requires disclosure.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">7. Scope, timeline and fees</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Fees depend on topic complexity, current stage, number/length of sessions, review material, urgency and deliverable format. The total fee for the confirmed scope must be communicated before payment. Hardware, components, shipping, software subscriptions, printing, travel and third-party charges are excluded unless explicitly included in writing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Timelines assume timely inputs and responses from the student. If the project direction changes materially, Silicon Geek may pause, requote or propose a revised plan. Cancellation and refund handling follows our <a href="/refund-cancellation-policy/">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">8. Clarifications and revisions</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Unless a different period is written in your booking, reasonable clarification on delivered guidance is available for <strong>[INSERT CLARIFICATION WINDOW, FOR EXAMPLE 7 DAYS]</strong> after the guidance is delivered. Clarification means explaining the same agreed material, correcting an error in our guidance or helping interpret a test result within the original checkpoint.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A new topic, new controller/board, major circuit redesign, additional chapter/module, fresh full-code rewrite, repeated failure caused by changed hardware or a new college requirement is new scope and may require a new quote/schedule.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">9. Hardware and result limitations</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Electronics debugging is evidence-based: a symptom can have multiple causes. Remote guidance depends on the photos, readings and information supplied and cannot prove that a physical circuit is safe or fully functional. Component clones, damaged sensors, weak batteries, loose jumpers, incompatible libraries and soldering faults may require physical testing or replacement.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Silicon Geek will give a logical test sequence and explain likely causes within scope, but does not guarantee that a particular purchased component, copied reference circuit or last-minute implementation will work. For mains/high-voltage/high-power systems, physical supervision by a qualified person is mandatory.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">10. Ownership, references and reuse</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The student remains responsible for the originality and authorship of work submitted to an institution. Sample explanations, diagrams or snippets provided during guidance should be understood, adapted where appropriate, tested and cited as required by institutional rules and licences. Open-source libraries and third-party assets retain their original licences and attribution requirements.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Silicon Geek may reuse general teaching explanations or anonymised problem patterns to improve future educational content, but will not publish identifiable student work or testimonials as marketing without appropriate permission.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">11. Confidentiality and data</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Material shared for guidance will be handled for service delivery, support, security and records as described in our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Do not send highly confidential institutional/company material unless you have written authority to share it and the handling method has been agreed in advance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">12. Right to pause or refuse service</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We may pause or decline help if information is repeatedly incomplete, the deadline/scope is unrealistic, communication becomes abusive, payment is fraudulent, a safety risk is ignored, or the request requires academic misconduct. Any paid undelivered portion will be reviewed under the Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy and applicable law.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">13. Before requesting help, confirm</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:list {"className":"cs-checklist"} --><ul class="wp-block-list cs-checklist"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>I want guidance so that I can learn and explain this project myself.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>I will share my real stage, errors, readings and guide requirements.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>I understand that components, tools and physical building/testing are mine unless expressly included.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>I understand there is no guarantee of approval, marks or a working outcome without my correct implementation and testing.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>I have read the Academic Integrity, Refund &amp; Cancellation and Privacy policies.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->

